      "summaries": {
        "en": "Perplexica is an open-source AI search engine that enhances traditional web searches by providing direct, context-aware answers instead of just links. It combines retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) with large language models to fetch and synthesize information from multiple sources in real-time. Developers can deploy it locally for private searches, integrate it into applications for intelligent Q&A features, or customize its search pipelines to handle domain-specific queries with improved accuracy.",
        "zh": "Perplexica 是一个开源 AI 搜索引擎，它通过检索增强生成技术，将传统搜索的链接列表转化为直接、准确的答案。其核心在于实时从多个来源获取信息，并利用大语言模型进行综合与精炼，确保回答既相关又可信。你可以将其部署为本地私有搜索工具，避免数据泄露风险；或集成到应用中，为用户提供智能问答功能；还能自定义检索流程，针对特定领域优化查询效果，非常适合构建知识库助手或研究辅助工具。",
        "es": "Perplexica is an open-source AI search engine that enhances traditional web searches by providing direct, context-aware answers instead of just links. It combines retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) with large language models to fetch and synthesize information from multiple sources in real-time. Developers can deploy it locally for private searches, integrate it into applications for intelligent Q&A features, or customize its search pipelines to handle domain-specific queries with improved accuracy.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "Perplexica stands out for ai-agents, ai-search-engine, and answering-engine in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Perplexica is an open-source AI search engine that enhances traditional web searches by providing direct, context-aware answers instead of just links. It combines retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) with large language models to fetch and synthesize information from multiple sources in real-time. Developers can deploy it locally for private searches, integrate it into applications for intelligent Q&A features, or customize its search pipelines to handle domain-specific queries with improved accuracy.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/ItzCrazyKns/Perplexica for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
